<<
/Title (This rule scales infinitely: a chord with a certain number of notes has that same number of possible positions \(1 root position, plus one inversion for every note above the root\). A triad \(3 notes\) = 3 positions. A 7th chord \(4 notes\) = 4 positions. A 9th chord \(5 notes\) would have 5 positions, and so on.)
/Dest [44 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 8849 0 R
/Next 8857 0 R
>>
